<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The assistant role's declaration. Brief section 1.1.

    Every attribute here is load-bearing, and two of them are load-bearing in a
    way that fails silently if they are wrong. From docs/research/R1.md, AOSP
    branch android16-release, read 2026-09-13:

    - recognitionService is mandatory. VoiceInteractionServiceInfo refuses the
      service outright with "No recognitionService specified", and the role
      observer in VoiceInteractionManagerService writes an empty string into
      Settings.Secure.ASSISTANT and VOICE_INTERACTION_SERVICE when it is
      missing. The app then holds the role, the picker shows it selected, and
      no gesture ever arrives.

    - supportsAssist must be true. The role observer skips any interactor
      service whose getSupportsAssist() is false and falls back to looking for
      an ACTION_ASSIST activity in the package, which would make Maia an
      assist-activity assistant with no session at all.

    supportsLaunchVoiceAssistFromKeyguard is deliberately absent rather than
    false. Brief section 1.1: it is claimed only if step 0 finds this build's
    keyguard exposes a voice affordance, and step 0 needs the phone.

    settingsActivity points at MainActivity until Maia has settings, as the
    brief says.
-->
<voice-interaction-service
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:recognitionService="dev.maia.app.assist.MaiaRecognitionService"
    android:sessionService="dev.maia.app.assist.MaiaSessionService"
    android:settingsActivity="dev.maia.app.MainActivity"
    android:supportsAssist="true" />
